    "summary": "Epic Truckin' → The Other One → Morning Dew marathon, high‑energy NYE classic",
    "blurb": "The show shines with a monster Truckin' > The Other One > Morning Dew sequence and strong renditions of Playing In The Band and Sugar Magnolia. Jerry’s guitar is hot throughout, Bill drives the jams with tight drumming, and Keith adds texture after the drum break. Overall a high‑energy New Year’s Eve performance that stands out in the 1972 catalog.",
    "review": "The Winterland NYE show of December 31 1972 finds the Dead firing on all cylinders as they charge into the second set with a blistering Truckin' that morphs seamlessly into an extended The Other One, culminating in a soaring Morning Dew. Jerry’s Strat is on fire, delivering searing leads and a relentless drive that pushes the jam forward, while Phil lays down inventive bass lines that lock tightly with Bill’s hot, propulsive drumming—especially during the drum‑bass interlude that fuels the middle section. Keith’s keyboards slip in after the drums, adding just enough texture to keep the momentum flowing without stealing the spotlight. The first set provides a solid foundation with tight renditions of Playing In The Band and Sugar Magnolia, and the encore closes the night on an uplifting note with Uncle John’s Band and One More Saturday Night. Across multiple soundboard sources the performance is captured cleanly, but the bertha‑ashley SBD stands out for its crispness and balance, presenting the marathon jam in vivid detail while preserving the raw excitement of that historic night.",
